cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or extend Hakem, please cite it as below. / Hakem'i kullanır ya da geliştirirseniz lütfen aşağıdaki gibi atıf yapın."
title: "Hakem: A Kernel-Checked Writing System for Machine Reasoning"
abstract: >-
  Hakem is a small language in which models (human or AI) write theories,
  glossaries, analogies, claims, proofs and counterexamples, together with a
  checker whose soundness is proved once, in the Lean 4 kernel, for every
  possible document. It is intended as shared infrastructure for automating
  the oversight of autonomous AI learning across disciplines.
authors:
  - alias: kimahmet
    website: "https://github.com/kimahmet"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kimahmet/hakem"
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.3.0"
date-released: "2026-11-27"
keywords:
  - verification
  - Lean 4
  - autonomous learning
  - AI oversight
  - analogy
  - is-ought
  - de Bruijn criterion
